{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889554-what-is-origins","id":889554,"title":"What is Origins","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-12T19:13:21-07:00","id":889554,"title":"What is Origins","content":"The last update mentioned that Origins was in it's first draft. What is that book about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>in any fight<br /> it is the guy who is willing to die<br /> who is going to win that inch.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BlackRoleplayersOrganization\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/BlackRoleplayersOrganization</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1402-kael-winters","name":"Kael Winters","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1402_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T22:32:19-07:00","id":889664,"title":"","content":"Scion: Origins is the book for Scions before their Visitation. It's the book that will have most of the basic systems in it, allowing more Hero-specific things to be focused on in Scion: Hero rather than using up word count for the general stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T23:55:34-07:00","id":889707,"title":"","content":"Power/genre wise it's &quot;urban fantasy&quot; level as I understand it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T19:27:27-07:00","id":890344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889554-what-is-origins?p=889664#post889664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scion: Origins is the book for Scions before their Visitation. It's the book that will have most of the basic systems in it, allowing more Hero-specific things to be focused on in Scion: Hero rather than using up word count for the general stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So it's more the fluff material so that the Hero book can focus on the meat of the game? Just to be on the same page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>in any fight<br /> it is the guy who is willing to die<br /> who is going to win that inch.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BlackRoleplayersOrganization\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/BlackRoleplayersOrganization</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1402-kael-winters","name":"Kael Winters","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1402_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T20:46:21-07:00","id":890381,"title":"","content":"Origins has all the base rules. Like Combat. And Skills. Character Creation. That might be the &quot;meat&quot;. And it sets up a lower powered urban fantasy setting. The Scions in Origin are pre-Visitation. <br /> <br /> Hero is the expansion that takes things up the first notch to &quot;Legendary&quot; (as oppose to &quot;Mythic&quot;). So, most of the meaty core rules are back in Origins.<br /> <br /> Ah... Geeze, dunno why I am even bothering to write this. I'm pretty much writing off the whole thing and will be taking a bow and walking away from Scion when the new rules get past a tipping point of &quot;Scion that was&quot; vs. &quot;Scion that will be&quot; (which seems to be coming up soon.). A significant chunk of these changes are going to work for me, thematically or mechanically (did ANYONE think about how those Legend Pool rules would smash up flat against online play? Obviously not...)<br /> <br /> But, there, I hope, is the answer","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T00:38:00-07:00","id":890482,"title":"","content":"As opposed to the finally honed and balanced masterpiece that was 1st Edition Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T09:25:23-07:00","id":890611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889554-what-is-origins?p=890482#post890482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As opposed to the finally honed and balanced masterpiece that was 1st Edition Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never said that Scion 1 was anything other than a hot mess. It completely fell apart at Demigod. Any gaming past that point had to be handwaving the rules. It had hitches and starts at Hero. <br /> <br /> But it was, ultimately, a beautiful hot mess. And, yes, to a degree... even a significant degree, Scion 2 will carry over some of that. However, the &quot;improvements&quot; to the rules partake of the many many many problems that beset the &quot;rules avoidance&quot; scheme that is literally drenching the RPG market. (And, to a degree there has even been some backlash and some move towards a happy medium) There are reasons for rules in RPGs. There are reasons to avoid them in some situations. But, ultimately, rules are to create a level playing field and one aspect of that is handling the overall game so that players (and STs) with the strong personalities, high levels of creativity (particularly as regards the setting) and more knowledge of the source material don't completely overwhelm everyone else in a tsunami (all too often of complete BS). When rules are created to absent that instead of support it, you end up with a game that can end up being alienating. Exponentially so to most people new to RPGs but also to players who are going to feel like they are being steamrolled. It ends up with a sort of elitism and all that negativity that that entails. <br /> <br /> All that, I am sure, can be dealt with by many groups, particularly those of veteran players in long-standing groups. I'm sure my group could handle whatever the changes were, even where they are annoying and less functional than they could be otherwise. HOWEVER, we have all moved very far apart from each other, so our gaming has to occur online. Online gaming is not uncommon. Adding in mechanics that work very very well on a table top - like, I dunno, pools of tokens to which everyone has access, or making cards a part of play - but are going to be significantly difficult to implement in an online setting is close to deal-breaker. (Miniatures can get a pass in many games as those games have platforms set up to deal with them). <br /> <br /> Sure, we're smart folks and could come up with something. (Oh great, another thing to manage in addition to all the other pitfalls of roleplaying via Skype...) But, add that to the approach being taken in the rules, it's just going to end up not being worth the headaches when there are other games out there that are more mechanically balanced out.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I, like others, some of whom have been shouted down so vociferously that they have just given up and moved on, was hoping for a game that was more of a Scion with some of the gaping holes closed up and obvious mismatches smoothed out. Though Aynie, Watcher, etc. and I have had our differences in the past, their Scion 2.0 (which is more like Scion 1.5 now) is more along the lines of what I was hoping for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T09:30:47-07:00","id":890615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889554-what-is-origins?p=890611#post890611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Never said that Scion 1 was anything other than a hot mess. It completely fell apart at Demigod. Any gaming past that point had to be handwaving the rules. It had hitches and starts at Hero.<br /> <br /> But it was, ultimately, a beautiful hot mess. And, yes, to a degree... even a significant degree, Scion 2 will carry over some of that. However, the &quot;improvements&quot; to the rules partake of the many many many problems that beset the &quot;rules avoidance&quot; scheme that is literally drenching the RPG market. (And, to a degree there has even been some backlash and some move towards a happy medium) There are reasons for rules in RPGs. There are reasons to avoid them in some situations. But, ultimately, rules are to create a level playing field and one aspect of that is handling the overall game so that players (and STs) with the strong personalities, high levels of creativity (particularly as regards the setting) and more knowledge of the source material don't completely overwhelm everyone else in a tsunami (all too often of complete BS). When rules are created to absent that instead of support it, you end up with a game that can end up being alienating. Exponentially so to most people new to RPGs but also to players who are going to feel like they are being steamrolled. It ends up with a sort of elitism and all that negativity that that entails.<br /> <br /> All that, I am sure, can be dealt with by many groups, particularly those of veteran players in long-standing groups. I'm sure my group could handle whatever the changes were, even where they are annoying and less functional than they could be otherwise. HOWEVER, we have all moved very far apart from each other, so our gaming has to occur online. Online gaming is not uncommon. Adding in mechanics that work very very well on a table top - like, I dunno, pools of tokens to which everyone has access, or making cards a part of play - but are going to be significantly difficult to implement in an online setting is close to deal-breaker. (Miniatures can get a pass in many games as those games have platforms set up to deal with them).<br /> <br /> Sure, we're smart folks and could come up with something. (Oh great, another thing to manage in addition to all the other pitfalls of roleplaying via Skype...) But, add that to the approach being taken in the rules, it's just going to end up not being worth the headaches when there are other games out there that are more mechanically balanced out.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I, like others, some of whom have been shouted down so vociferously that they have just given up and moved on, was hoping for a game that was more of a Scion with some of the gaping holes closed up and obvious mismatches smoothed out. Though Aynie, Watcher, etc. and I have had our differences in the past, their Scion 2.0 (which is more like Scion 1.5 now) is more along the lines of what I was hoping for.</div> </div> </div> </div>im afraid i don't understand,what exactly do you disagree about the new system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T09:34:13-07:00","id":890618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889554-what-is-origins?p=890615#post890615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">im afraid i don't understand,what exactly do you disagree about the new system?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I've already come close to thread-jacking (though my last post is about &quot;What Is Origins?&quot;, 'm pretty sure it's not what the OP was actually asking for.) If you'd like to discuss my concerns more full, feel free to private message me and I'll try to articulate them more fully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T10:01:14-07:00","id":890628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889554-what-is-origins?p=890611#post890611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that, I am sure, can be dealt with by many groups, particularly those of veteran players in long-standing groups. I'm sure my group could handle whatever the changes were, even where they are annoying and less functional than they could be otherwise. HOWEVER, we have all moved very far apart from each other, so our gaming has to occur online. Online gaming is not uncommon. Adding in mechanics that work very very well on a table top - like, I dunno, pools of tokens to which everyone has access, or making cards a part of play - but are going to be significantly difficult to implement in an online setting is close to deal-breaker. (Miniatures can get a pass in many games as those games have platforms set up to deal with them).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how anything in Scion 2e is going to be difficult to implement in an online game, assuming everyone keeps track of their pools. Fate does just fine online.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, add that to the approach being taken in the rules, it's just going to end up not being worth the headaches when there are other games out there that are more mechanically balanced out. </div> </div> </div>Scion 2e's rules aren't fully written yet, much less balanced out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, I, like others, some of whom have been shouted down so vociferously that they have just given up and moved on, was hoping for a game that was more of a Scion with some of the gaping holes closed up and obvious mismatches smoothed out. Though Aynie, Watcher, etc. and I have had our differences in the past, their Scion 2.0 (which is more like Scion 1.5 now) is more along the lines of what I was hoping for. </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry you feel that way, but a patch wouldn't solve Scion 1e's core fundamental issues. Scion 2.0 is excellent and I admire that team's work, but they're building on a rotten foundation. You're not wrong in calling it Scion 1.5.<br /> <br /> Better to rip the whole thing out and rebuild it.<br /> <br /> Ajax, I'm sorry if some of the rules so far don't please you, but there will be a rules release around the time of the Kickstarter after some playtesting has been done, so you can judge for yourself. Online play is something I take pretty seriously since it's the primary way I play tabletop games nowadays too. If you've got concerns, feel free to reach out to me and say something or start a thread. A number of the playtesters I've talked to are online-only so far, so I think any issues with online play will get brought up so we can address them and smooth them out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 05-14-2016, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T10:02:02-07:00","id":890629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kael Winters</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889554-what-is-origins?p=890344#post890344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it's more the fluff material so that the Hero book can focus on the meat of the game? Just to be on the same page.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just the opposite; it's a lot of the core rules and setting material, so Hero can focus on the Scions themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T13:47:00-07:00","id":890766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889554-what-is-origins?p=890628#post890628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry you feel that way, but a patch wouldn't solve Scion 1e's core fundamental issues. Scion 2.0 is excellent and I admire that team's work, but they're building on a rotten foundation. You're not wrong in calling it Scion 1.5.<br /> <br /> Better to rip the whole thing out and rebuild it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>We discussed the future of Scion 2.0 when Scion 2nd Ed. first was announced, and decided that if the new system was palatable to our tastes, we would do our best to round up the core rules that we had - finish the Purviews in Mechanical Editing phase, and end it there. We loved Scion 1st edition, but the base was so broken that having to rebuild it from the bottom up was more effort than we could manage as a small team and with full time school and jobs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T22:28:08-07:00","id":893859,"title":"","content":"I like that the actual developer takes the time to convince one mopey guy to stick with the game. That right there is dedication.<br /> <br /> I for one am super jazzed about Scion 2E. I played a bunch of games using the original rules without a hiccup, and look forward to doing more of the same thanks to a passionate team. I think Origins is a rad idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","name":"Foxcalibur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T13:48:10-07:00","id":894294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foxcalibur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889554-what-is-origins?p=893859#post893859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I for one am super jazzed about Scion 2E. I played a bunch of games using the original rules without a hiccup, and look forward to doing more of the same thanks to a passionate team. I think Origins is a rad idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, man, you might not feel so optimistic after you see the Panther Titan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T14:28:19-07:00","id":894321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889554-what-is-origins?p=894294#post894294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, man, you might not feel so optimistic after you see the Panther Titan.</div> </div> </div> </div>What the Christ would such a Titan's deal be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","name":"Foxcalibur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T16:02:27-07:00","id":894381,"title":"","content":"It combines with four other Animal Titans to make the Titan Megazord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T13:23:09-07:00","id":896259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foxcalibur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889554-what-is-origins?p=893859#post893859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like that the actual developer takes the time to convince one mopey guy to stick with the game. That right there is dedication.<br /> <br /> I for one am super jazzed about Scion 2E. I played a bunch of games using the original rules without a hiccup, and look forward to doing more of the same thanks to a passionate team. I think Origins is a rad idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the &quot;one mopey guy&quot; ----- There is a quality management truism that if one person is speaking up with a concern, there are at least a dozen other people who feel exactly the same way who remain silent. There are probably close to a dozen of what used to be power posters, people with a deep and abiding love of Scion's core concepts and even its quirky conceits, people who are actually credentialed experts in relevant fields, who have almost completely faded out, some from just this board and others from the OP boards altogether. At least a few of those were browbeaten into leaving for not being &quot;super jazzed&quot; about Scion-New, which is definitely &quot;passionate&quot; but probably in all the wrong ways. <br /> <br /> So, there's that. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T13:31:16-07:00","id":896268,"title":"","content":"Hey, I'm sorry you were brow-beaten. That's the worst. Your posts read as the sort of thing which inspires people on other forums to ask &quot;Can I have your stuff?&quot; but I was certainly being glib <b>and I'm sorry</b>. You just sounded a bit Droopy Dog about the whole thing. But I understand your frustration. Not all new editions are good edition. 5th Edition D&amp;D, for example, is a tire fire. I for one am just happy we're getting more and new Scion and that a passionate team seems to be working on it.<br /> <br /> Of course, I tend to outright ignore rules and ideas I don't like, and just squeeze the juicy delicious pulp out of a new edition to get a campaign that squares with what I want. That way, I'm never disappointed and any new edition of a game I like has something for me.<br /> <br /> Except for 5th Edition D&amp;D. It is truly the worst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11816,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","user":"Foxcalibur","date":".  To add an actual apology for being abrasive. 05-22-2016, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11816-foxcalibur","name":"Foxcalibur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T13:52:26-07:00","id":896286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889554-what-is-origins?p=890628#post890628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see how anything in Scion 2e is going to be difficult to implement in an online game, assuming everyone keeps track of their pools. Fate does just fine online.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Scion 2e's rules aren't fully written yet, much less balanced out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm sorry you feel that way, but a patch wouldn't solve Scion 1e's core fundamental issues. Scion 2.0 is excellent and I admire that team's work, but they're building on a rotten foundation. You're not wrong in calling it Scion 1.5.<br /> <br /> Better to rip the whole thing out and rebuild it.<br /> <br /> Ajax, I'm sorry if some of the rules so far don't please you, but there will be a rules release around the time of the Kickstarter after some playtesting has been done, so you can judge for yourself. Online play is something I take pretty seriously since it's the primary way I play tabletop games nowadays too. If you've got concerns, feel free to reach out to me and say something or start a thread. A number of the playtesters I've talked to are online-only so far, so I think any issues with online play will get brought up so we can address them and smooth them out.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience and as far as I have been able to tell by reaching out to those I know, Fate doesn't do well as Fate online. It does Fate as a DRPG. (Which admittedly is a lot like what Fate is anyways.) The difficult to manage mechanic get dropped. Which is problematic if the mechanic is core. From the material I have read there is a grouping aspect to these tokens that would be effortless at a table FTF but is going to require some creative workaround to manage online. If I am not getting the rules involved or there has been a change since that bit was published, I apologize, but our group was looking through the bits that are out there and it kept coming up.<br /> <br /> Since I'm not a playtester or a developer, I can only address what you have posted for us to read. I'm going on that. It's not like looking at the bits of Wraith20 that come out. There's no context to fall back on. This is all new from the ground up. All I can understand is what you have put out there and the comments the developers make afterwards. So I know I'm not getting an accurate read, but it's the only read I CAN get. And rules like Consolation and mantles are worrisome from what I have seen. Consolation seems like a bad idea all around. It's not setting appropriate. What Consolation did Icarus get? Orpheus? Sigurd? Balder? Miach? Etc. Consolation seems to remove actual failure from the equations. Sometimes myths aren't about &quot;failing forward&quot;. They're about failing. Catastrophically. Mantles might be the salvation of the game, but they could could just as easily make it very much like the worst aspects of Fate, e.g. he who has the best bullshit wins. The new Virtues seem so vague as to be be ethereal. Old Virtues had their problems, but they were an actual THING, with benefits and drawbacks that had an effect. The could be played up or played down, but they were THERE. The new ones? I don't see them as being anything other than a background concept that can possibly be referenced when it seems appropriate, but, really, not often. <br /> <br /> The core system of Scion 1.0 was a cobbled together mess. I agree. It was built on the White Wolf engine with parts of Adventure bolted on here, Aberrant spliced in there, Exalted threaded through some of the gaps like twine, etc. But that's different than completely rotten. I can't buy that. It's based on the White Wolff engine and, to one degree or another, that's been functioning through several game lines for over twenty years. If you want to go a whole other direction, that's fine, but that doesn't mean that Scion couldn't have been reworked from the ground up from the fundamentals, From my days as a lawyer, I can easily understand going another direction for purely IP reasons or taking that hat off, for purely creative reasons, but I don't think that it was actually impossible. Whether or not I agreed with everything they were doing, Watcher, Aynie, et al. were trying to do so fairly successfully.<br /> <br /> I'm not giving up 100% (though I have thought about about and have discussed it with those who have), but my eye is wary one at this point. I don't think my concerns are unreasonable. As you have said, this IS going to be a completely different game with, essentially the same name and some fundamental conceits in common. That IS a big change to make. CoD isn't really the NWOD, just like 2nd Ed. AD&amp;D isn't really 3rd or 3.5 which are not 4th or 5th. Scion 1 and Scion 2 are going to be a similar shift. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T14:57:44-07:00","id":896324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889554-what-is-origins?p=896286#post896286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CoD isn't really the NWOD, just like 2nd Ed. AD&amp;D isn't really 3rd or 3.5 which are not 4th or 5th. Scion 1 and Scion 2 are going to be a similar shift.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't really say that the move from nWoD to CofD is anywhere near the same as an edition change in D&amp;D; 99% percent of old material can easily be converted to the new with a tiny bit of work, and the fluff is almost wholly untouched.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T14:06:18-07:00","id":897163,"title":"","content":"hell most of the material can be outright stolen into second. It's not like I need an entire new monster manual for chronicles, although I wouldn't mind it at all if we rolled one out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T20:13:59-07:00","id":897515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889554-what-is-origins?p=896286#post896286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> From the material I have read there is a grouping aspect to these tokens that would be effortless at a table FTF but is going to require some creative workaround to manage online.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Okay guys, I've got this page [here] that has a Google Spreadsheet that has the Initiative Spread, as well as the public pools. Keep it tabbed while you play, alright?&quot;<br /> <br /> To be a little less glib, I looked over the Alpha Slice, and I didn't actually see anything that jumped out at me as &quot;This is going to be impossible to run in online games&quot;. I'll need to do some fiddling and poking at it, of course, but nothing glaring smacked me in the face.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Old Virtues had their problems, but they were an actual THING, with benefits and drawbacks that had an effect. The could be played up or played down, but they were THERE. The new ones? I don't see them as being anything other than a background concept that can possibly be referenced when it seems appropriate, but, really, not often. </div> </div> </div>The new edition of Exalted tossed out the old Virtues in favor of placing a bigger emphasis on the Intimacy system. Having played it, it feels much better, even without the potential bonus dice from Virtue Channels. And that game had just four Virtues to keep straight, while Scion had how many? I want to say 12-16. Having run a couple Scion games, none of my players used their Virtues.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foxcalibur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889554-what-is-origins?p=896268#post896268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except for 5th Edition D&amp;D. It is truly the worst.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I <i>like</i> 5th Edition. I'd ask what's wrong with it, but...<br /> <br /> Eh, if you want to rant, fire me a PM and we'll talk more there. Keeping on-topic and all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T09:58:07-07:00","id":897911,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Kyman201;n897515]<br /> <br /> &quot;Okay guys, I've got this page [here] that has a Google Spreadsheet that has the Initiative Spread, as well as the public pools. Keep it tabbed while you play, alright?&quot;<br /> <br /> To be a little less glib, I looked over the Alpha Slice, and I didn't actually see anything that jumped out at me as &quot;This is going to be impossible to run in online games&quot;. I'll need to do some fiddling and poking at it, of course, but nothing glaring smacked me in the face.<br /> <br /> The new edition of Exalted tossed out the old Virtues in favor of placing a bigger emphasis on the Intimacy system. Having played it, it feels much better, even without the potential bonus dice from Virtue Channels. And that game had just four Virtues to keep straight, while Scion had how many? I want to say 12-16. Having run a couple Scion games, none of my players used their Virtues.<br /> <br /> /QUOTE]<br /> <br /> RE: Tokens by Google - Messy. Unnecessary. Could have been avoided effortlessly. It doesn't appreciably add to the feel of the game mechanically or by achieving the goals of a game about living through the creation of new myths. Most myths when the demigods and heroes got together in groups aren't about the group's accomplishment in any case. It's about the amazing things each member does that contribute to the goal (vide the Argonauts or the 108 Stars).<br /> <br /> RE: Virtues, New and Old - Just because you didn't use them doesn't mean others didn't and they didn't add appreciably to the games. They did in the ones I ran and in the ones I played in. They made the character of each pantheon very distinctive and something that HAD to be taken into account in gameplay. Having a sheet of those Virtues reduced to bullet points was MUCH easier than the proposed online token tracking system. The new Virtue system is going to move the whole idea into the background and color it with appreciable amounts of vagueness. More like D&amp;D games where alignment was a couple of letters on a character sheet and rarely referenced. (Not that it COULDN'T be important, but it just wasn't almost all the time). Probably even more vaguel than that. More like Essence in Mage. That is out there but so intangible as to be hard to even bring into play without a lot of effort. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:17:03-07:00","id":897940,"title":"","content":"I understand your views on what we have seen so far of Scion 2E, Ajax. At the moment, I am still wanting to see the new books before deciding what to do on that front.<br /> Until then, there is still Scion 1E and a few other games that come close-ish to the material (Part-Time Gods, for one). Best of luck with what you choose.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:39:46-07:00","id":897966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PHGraves</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/889554-what-is-origins?p=897940#post897940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand your views on what we have seen so far of Scion 2E, Ajax. At the moment, I am still wanting to see the new books before deciding what to do on that front.<br /> Until then, there is still Scion 1E and a few other games that come close-ish to the material (Part-Time Gods, for one). Best of luck with what you choose.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be &quot;Mage 20&quot; while keeping a weather eye on Scion as it develops. Then we'll see, (Maybe the Wraith Curse will loosen up enough to get that bad boy out and about.... but talking a couple of reluctant newer players into that would probably be more difficult than trying another Scion game.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}